#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *Assam Accord Cutoff Date:* Strictly *24 March 1971* (eve of Bangladesh war), NOT 15 August 1947 or 26 January 1950.
  2. *Punjab Accord Signatory:* Signed between Rajiv Gandhi and *Sant Harchand Singh Longowal*, NOT Jarnail Singh Bhindranwale (who died in Blue Star).
  3. *Mizo vs Naga Rebel Leaders:* *Laldenga* led the Mizo National Front (MNF); *Angami Zapu Phizo* led the Naga National Council (NNC).
  4. *Inquiry Commission for 1984 Riots:* *Justice G.T. Nanavati Commission* (2000), NOT the Shah Commission (which investigated the 1975–77 Emergency).
  5. *Regional Film Icons:* *N.T. Rama Rao (NTR)* founded TDP in Andhra Pradesh (1982); *M.G. Ramachandran (MGR)* founded AIADMK in Tamil Nadu (1972).
  6. *First North-East Tribal State:* *Nagaland* (created in 1963), NOT Meghalaya (1972) or Mizoram (1987).
  7. *Accommodation vs Assimilation:* India rejected *cultural assimilation* (melting pot); it adopted *democratic accommodation* (mosaic).
]

