= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Fifteen authentic CUET UG examination-standard multiple-choice questions testing conceptual, chronological, institutional, and factual mastery. Marking scheme: $+5$ for correct answer, $-1$ for incorrect attempt.

== Part 1: Kashmir Accession, Punjab Crisis & 1984 Violence

#mcq(1, [In October 1947, who was the Maharaja of Jammu and Kashmir who signed the Instrument of Accession with the Dominion of India?], (
  [Maharaja Gulab Singh], [Maharaja Hari Singh], [Sheikh Abdullah], [Karan Singh],
))

#solution(1, [Maharaja Hari Singh was the Hindu monarch of Jammu and Kashmir who signed the Instrument of Accession on 26 October 1947 following the armed Pakistani tribal invasion.], answer: [B])

#mcq(2, [In which year did the Shiromani Akali Dal pass the historic Anandpur Sahib Resolution demanding greater state autonomy and federal restructuring?], (
  [1966], [1971], [1973], [1984],
))

#solution(2, [The Anandpur Sahib Resolution was passed by the Akali Dal in October 1973, demanding federal restructuring, river water reallocation, and greater state autonomy.], answer: [C])

#mcq(3, [Operation Blue Star, the Indian Army's military operation to flush out armed militants from the Golden Temple complex in Amritsar, was conducted in:], (
  [June 1984], [October 1984], [July 1985], [January 1986],
))

#solution(3, [Operation Blue Star was conducted by the Indian armed forces in June 1984 to eliminate armed religious extremists led by Jarnail Singh Bhindranwale from the Golden Temple complex.], answer: [A])

#mcq(4, [The historic Punjab Accord (Memorandum of Settlement) of July 1985 was signed between Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi and which moderate Akali Dal leader?], (
  [Jarnail Singh Bhindranwale], [Parkash Singh Badal], [Sant Harchand Singh Longowal], [Gurcharan Singh Tohra],
))

#solution(4, [Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi signed the historic Memorandum of Settlement in July 1985 with Sant Harchand Singh Longowal, President of the Shiromani Akali Dal.], answer: [C])

#mcq(5, [The Mizo National Front (MNF), which launched a two-decade armed insurgency following the 1959 Mautam famine, was founded and led by:], (
  [Angami Zapu Phizo], [Laldenga], [Prafulla Kumar Mahanta], [Bhrigu Kumar Phukan],
))

#solution(5, [Laldenga founded the Mizo National Front (MNF) following the 1959 Mautam famine and led the armed rebellion before signing the 1986 Mizo Peace Accord to become Chief Minister.], answer: [B])

#pagebreak()
== Part 2: North-East Accords, Cutoff Dates & Regional Parties

#mcq(6, [Under the Assam Accord signed on 15 August 1985 between the Central Government and AASU leaders, what was the cutoff date for the detection and deportation of illegal immigrants?], (
  [15 August 1947], [26 January 1950], [24 March 1971], [1 January 1980],
))

#solution(6, [The Assam Accord fixed midnight of 24 March 1971 (the eve of the Bangladesh Liberation War) as the strict cutoff date for identifying and deporting illegal immigrants.], answer: [C])

#mcq(7, [Which regional political party was founded in 1985 by student leaders following the conclusion of the six-year Assam movement against foreign nationals?], (
  [All Assam Students Union (AASU)], [Bodo People's Front (BPF)], [United Minorities Front (UMF)], [Asom Gana Parishad (AGP)],
))

#solution(7, [AASU leaders transformed their student movement into a formal regional political party named Asom Gana Parishad (AGP) in 1985, sweeping the state assembly elections.], answer: [D])

#mcq(8, [The Telugu Desam Party (TDP) was founded in 1982 on the platform of Telugu self-respect (Atma Gauravam) by which popular cultural and cinema icon?], (
  [N.T. Rama Rao (NTR)], [M.G. Ramachandran (MGR)], [Chiranjeevi], [K. Karunanidhi],
))

#solution(8, [N.T. Rama Rao (NTR), legendary Telugu cinema superstar, formed the Telugu Desam Party in 1982 on the platform of "Telugu Atma Gauravam", routing the Congress in Andhra Pradesh.], answer: [A])

#mcq(9, [Which state was created in 1963 as the first tribal state carved out of composite Assam in response to the armed Naga national movement?], (
  [Meghalaya], [Nagaland], [Mizoram], [Manipur],
))

#solution(9, [Nagaland was granted full statehood in 1963, becoming the first tribal state carved out from composite Assam to accommodate the Naga movement led by the NNC.], answer: [B])

#mcq(10, [Which judicial inquiry commission was appointed in 2000 to submit a comprehensive report investigating the 1984 anti-Sikh violence in Delhi and other states?], (
  [Sarkaria Commission], [Shah Commission], [Verma Commission], [The Justice G.T. Nanavati Commission],
))

#solution(10, [The Justice G.T. Nanavati Commission of Inquiry was appointed in 2000 by the NDA government to probe the 1984 anti-Sikh riots, indicting several influential figures.], answer: [D])

