== Part 3: Accords, Leaders & Constitutional Federalism

#mcq(11, [Under the historic 1974 Indira-Sheikh Accord, Sheikh Abdullah agreed to drop the demand for a plebiscite in Jammu and Kashmir in exchange for:], (
  [Assuming office as the Chief Minister of Jammu and Kashmir while recognizing J&K as an integral constituent unit of the Indian Union], [Creating an independent republic of Kashmir], [Merging Pakistan-Occupied Kashmir into India], [Abolishing Article 370 of the Indian Constitution],
))

#solution(11, [Under the 1974 Accord, Sheikh Abdullah renounced the demand for a plebiscite, affirmed Jammu and Kashmir as an integral part of India, and assumed office as Chief Minister.], answer: [A])

#mcq(12, [The Naga National Council (NNC), which declared the independence of Nagaland in August 1947 and launched an armed sovereignty movement, was led by:], (
  [Laldenga], [Prafulla Kumar Mahanta], [Angami Zapu Phizo], [Muivah],
))

#solution(12, [Angami Zapu Phizo was the legendary leader of the Naga National Council (NNC) who spearheaded the armed struggle for Naga independence from 1947 onwards.], answer: [C])

#mcq(13, [The Dravidian movement in southern India, which opposed northern Hindi linguistic dominance and advocated rationalism and social reform, was pioneered under the leadership of:], (
  [E.V. Ramasamy 'Periyar'], [C. Rajagopalachari], [K. Kamaraj], [M.G. Ramachandran],
))

#solution(13, [E.V. Ramasamy 'Periyar' pioneered the Dravidian movement through the Self-Respect Movement and Dravidar Kazhagam, combating caste hierarchies and Hindi imposition.], answer: [A])

#mcq(14, [Article 371A of the Constitution of India provides special constitutional protections for which northeastern state, safeguarding its customary laws and land ownership?], (
  [Assam], [Nagaland], [Mizoram], [Manipur],
))

#solution(14, [Article 371A provides special protective status for Nagaland, stipulating that no Act of Parliament respecting Naga customary law or religious practices applies without state assembly approval.], answer: [B])

#mcq(15, [How did the Indian constitutional model handle intense regional aspirations and ethnic assertions compared to traditional European nation-state models?], (
  [By enforcing strict linguistic and cultural homogenization through compulsory state schooling], [By expelling ethnic minorities to neighboring countries], [By abandoning federal democracy in favor of a unitary monarchy], [By adopting democratic accommodation and asymmetrical federalism rather than forced cultural and linguistic assimilation],
))

#solution(15, [India rejected the European assimilationist nation-state model, instead pioneering democratic accommodation, asymmetrical federalism (Articles 370, 371), and autonomous councils to protect regional diversities.], answer: [D])

